From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 11:25:34 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 13/15] optimizer: specialize bounded records, closures and
 scalar work

Propagate known closure targets through bounded parameter, phi and return
analysis while retaining actual environments. Permit bounded Static
Hermes inlining that exposes temporary records without imposing its
policy on other backends. Promote eligible helper arguments, distribute
unaliased branch-local object spreads and retain source evaluation order.

Add shared record-use/effect analysis and guarded data-property,
method-call, byte-array-loop and record-read transformations. Preserve
generic operations at their original points when a proof or guard fails.
Keep returned-record forwarding and late materialization outside the
default pipeline, and retain explicit activation for optional policies.

Prove bounded signed/unsigned integer ranges, eliminate redundant
conversions and lower supported numeric Math operations directly.
Optionally retain proved integer temporaries in native registers, checking
every definition and consumer while preserving boxing and generic coercion.

Share guarded string-index comparisons and immutable lengths. Support
invocation-scoped reuse of proved string/scan helpers with bounded keys,
misses and retained backing storage; copy eligible result arrays rather
than exposing cached identity. Guard array predicate lowering without
removing holes, inherited reads, mutations or callback exceptions.

Keep pass registration, compiler options, runtime-helper consumers and
optimizer/native fixtures together. Optional transformations retain their
documented embedding assumptions and do not imply a measured speedup.
